IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `doga-owner`
IMPORT `doga-qa`

-- Dog Act 1976 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (doga-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and every
-- situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error ("it
-- is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with FALSE and every
-- later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. For the owner (the baseline's seat) each answer is also asserted
-- equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same facts. Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited
-- text, never copied from the output.
--
-- Facts: Chloe and Mochi (c075), with the baseline's dogs (doga-cases-owner.l4), restated here. As there, Mochi's age,
-- breed and papers are ASSUMED; the other dogs are the encoder's illustrations.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked dog` IS A Dog
ASSUME `an unasked term` IS A Term
ASSUME `an unasked place` IS A Place
ASSUME `an unasked control` IS A Control
ASSUME `an unasked incident` IS AN Incident

`as the owner` MEANS `I own or keep a dog`
`as the person attacked` MEANS `A dog has attacked, chased or threatened me or my animal`

