-- Mirror cases: one incident and one dog, from the owner's seat and from the seat of the person attacked.
#ASSERT `Could my dog be declared a dangerous dog` `as the owner` `a chase that caused injury or damage` EQUALS `the answer is` `yes, if the local government or its authorised person is of the opinion that this is so (s 33E(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the dog that attacked, chased or threatened me be declared dangerous` `as the person attacked` `a chase that caused injury or damage` EQUALS `the answer is` `yes, if the local government or its authorised person is of the opinion that this is so (s 33E(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my dog a dangerous dog under the Act` `as the owner` `a pit bull cross` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is the dog already a dangerous dog under the Act` `as the person attacked` `a pit bull cross` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my dog lawfully where it is in this public place` `as the owner` `Mochi` `an ordinary public place` TRUE TRUE `held on a leash by a person able to control it` 3 FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `offence under s 31(3): a fine of up to $5 000, unless I took all reasonable precautions (s 33B)`
#ASSERT `Was the dog lawfully in the public place where it happened` `as the person attacked` `Mochi` `an ordinary public place` TRUE TRUE `held on a leash by a person able to control it` 3 FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `offence under s 31(3): a fine of up to $5 000, unless I took all reasonable precautions (s 33B)`

